WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.227 --> 00:00:25.513
Mama refused to change her mind about tennis camp. But on Sunday night after Iris and Javier washed the dishes, they started begging her.

2
00:00:25.514 --> 00:00:29.991
"Can't we stay with a friend?" Iris pleaded.

3
00:00:29.992 --> 00:00:37.506
"Or a neighbor?" Javier said. "Mrs. Jones is always home, and she lives right downstairs."

4
00:00:37.506 --> 00:00:43.258
Mama crossed her arms. "We can't impose on others like that."

5
00:00:43.259 --> 00:00:46.728
"What if Papa came home?" Iris asked.

6
00:00:46.729 --> 00:00:51.999
"Papa is not coming home, Iris," Mama said firmly.

7
00:00:51.999 --> 00:00:59.406
"And even if he did, he could just as easily walk out again. We can't depend on anyone else."

8
00:00:59.407 --> 00:01:06.810
She shook her head. "You two are going to tennis camp tomorrow, and that's final."

9
00:01:06.811 --> 00:01:10.874
"Can Iris and I go to the park?" Javier blurted out.

10
00:01:10.874 --> 00:01:14.050
Iris and Mama both looked at him.

11
00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:19.382
"Javier never wants to go to the park," Iris thought.

12
00:01:19.383 --> 00:01:26.206
"It's getting late, Javier," Mama said. "You have to get up early for camp tomorrow morning."

13
00:01:26.207 --> 00:01:31.706
"It's summertime," Javier said. "Please?"

14
00:01:31.707 --> 00:01:37.599
"Fine. But stay together, and I want you back here in an hour."

15
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:48.355
"No problem. Let's go, Iris." Javier waved Iris out the door, ignoring the confused look on her face.

16
00:01:48.356 --> 00:01:57.348
Once they were out in the hall, Iris poked her brother. "What's going on?"

17
00:01:57.349 --> 00:02:00.779
He shook his head. "At the park."

18
00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:07.711
"Fine." Iris followed him down the stairs.

19
00:02:07.711 --> 00:02:15.195
Outside, she jogged ahead, leaving Javier to try to keep up.

20
00:02:15.196 --> 00:02:23.504
She arrived at the park first and leaned against a bench to stretch her calves.

21
00:02:23.504 --> 00:02:29.558
A few moments later Javier flung himself on the bench, panting from his run.

22
00:02:29.559 --> 00:02:40.139
"We have to . . . think of a way . . . to get out of tennis camp. Mama's not going to change her mind."

23
00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:50.627
Iris had noticed a tennis court nearby and was watching some people play. "I think we're stuck playing tennis, Javier."

24
00:02:50.628 --> 00:02:57.626
Javier snorted. "I'd rather spend the week doing household chores than play tennis!"

25
00:02:57.627 --> 00:03:03.724
He squinted at the court. "Wait a minute. Is that Liam?"

26
00:03:03.725 --> 00:03:09.334
A kid from Javier's class waved and came over.

27
00:03:09.335 --> 00:03:18.625
"Hey, Javier," he said. Liam had a thick mop of red hair and a face full of freckles. "You're Iris, right?"

28
00:03:18.625 --> 00:03:27.196
Iris nodded. She and Javier were always in separate classes, but most of the kids at school knew they were twins.

29
00:03:27.197 --> 00:03:32.116
"Dude, since when do you play tennis?" Javier asked.

30
00:03:32.117 --> 00:03:39.250
Liam smiled. "My older sister, Molly, has been teaching me. She's on the high school team."

31
00:03:39.251 --> 00:03:51.173
"I taught him everything he knows." A taller, even brighter-haired version of Liam joined them. "I'm Molly."

32
00:03:51.174 --> 00:03:59.158
"Our mom signed us up for tennis camp," Javier said with a groan. "It starts tomorrow."

33
00:03:59.159 --> 00:04:05.248
"I'm really into soccer," Iris added. "I don't know anything about tennis."

34
00:04:05.249 --> 00:04:08.241
"Me neither," Javier said.

35
00:04:08.242 --> 00:04:17.219
"I can show you some of the basics." Molly handed Javier her racket and headed across the court.

36
00:04:17.219 --> 00:04:22.209
"Ball, racket, swing. That's all you need to know to start."

37
00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:27.484
Javier stepped onto the court and held the racket like a sword.

38
00:04:27.485 --> 00:04:38.814
When Molly hit the ball to him, he swung his racket in a wide arc, just tipping the ball, which dropped to the ground at his feet.

39
00:04:38.815 --> 00:04:45.948
He gave it several more tries before finally handing the racket back to Molly.

40
00:04:45.949 --> 00:04:50.043
"Thanks, but I stink at this," he said.

41
00:04:50.044 --> 00:04:53.361
"How about you?" Molly asked Iris.

42
00:04:53.361 --> 00:05:00.368
"It can't be that hard," Iris thought. After all, she was a good athlete.

43
00:05:00.369 --> 00:05:09.853
Iris took the racket and waited for Molly to serve a ball to her. Iris swung hard—and missed.

44
00:05:09.854 --> 00:05:13.479
The force of her swing spun her in a full circle.

45
00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:21.000
Javier laughed and so did Liam, though Liam quickly tried to cover it up.

46
00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:27.006
Heat spread up the back of Iris' neck as she tried to hit the ball again and again.

47
00:05:27.007 --> 00:05:39.495
Finally, after a particularly epic miss, everyone laughed hard. This time Iris herself had to join in.

48
00:05:39.496 --> 00:05:46.320
"Well, I stink at this too, Javier." She handed the racket back to Molly.

49
00:05:46.321 --> 00:05:50.118
"I guess my soccer skills aren't going to help me with tennis!"

50
00:05:50.119 --> 00:05:54.750
Liam shrugged. "I'm sure you'll learn to play at camp."

51
00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:59.016
"Yeah." Molly nodded. "Camp will be fun."

52
00:05:59.017 --> 00:06:03.490
"That reminds me." Javier nudged Iris.

53
00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:12.054
"We have some planning to do." He waved to Liam and Molly. "Later."

54
00:06:12.055 --> 00:06:18.307
The twins stepped off the court. "That was the worst," Javier said.

55
00:06:18.308 --> 00:06:20.535
Iris nodded glumly.

56
00:06:20.536 --> 00:06:26.960
"We have to get out of camp somehow," Javier went on. "Got any bright ideas?"

57
00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:33.102
"Not yet," Iris said. "But I'll try to think of something."

58
00:06:33.103 --> 00:06:38.688
The next morning the twins still had no plan for getting out of tennis camp.

59
00:06:38.689 --> 00:06:47.943
Mama was getting ready for work, but she had left out cereal and milk for breakfast, and bread and cheese for sandwiches to bring to camp.

60
00:06:47.944 --> 00:06:57.538
Javier drummed his fingers on the table as Iris slurped down her last mouthful of cereal.

61
00:06:57.539 --> 00:07:01.347
"What are we going to—" Javier froze.

62
00:07:01.347 --> 00:07:07.771
Iris looked up. Javier was staring at the bread and cheese next to their lunch bags.

63
00:07:07.772 --> 00:07:17.258
"I have an idea!" Javier grinned. "Just follow my lead. I'll make our lunches while you wash our breakfast dishes."

64
00:07:17.259 --> 00:07:21.334
"Huh?" Iris shot him a questioning look.

65
00:07:21.335 --> 00:07:30.153
Still, she carried the bowls to the sink and washed them while Javier prepared their sandwiches and water bottles.

66
00:07:30.154 --> 00:07:40.139
He was still busy when she went off to brush her teeth, but when she walked into the living room a few minutes later, their backpacks sat ready beside the front door.

67
00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:45.484
Javier slung his over his shoulder, and Iris did the same.

68
00:07:45.485 --> 00:07:49.151
"Ready to go to the bus stop?" Javier asked.

69
00:07:49.151 --> 00:07:50.190
"Yep."

70
00:07:50.191 --> 00:07:55.640
Mama stepped into the hallway and straightened her skirt.

71
00:07:55.640 --> 00:08:02.886
"I'm leaving for work in a few minutes." She blew them a kiss. "Have a good day at camp."

72
00:08:02.887 --> 00:08:09.783
"Bye," Iris said. "A good day would be a miracle," she thought.

73
00:08:09.784 --> 00:08:16.790
"You did what?" Iris turned to Javier once they'd reached the bus stop.

74
00:08:16.791 --> 00:08:24.758
"I thought leaving our lunches behind would be a good excuse for missing the bus." Javier wiped a hand over his forehead.

75
00:08:24.759 --> 00:08:28.606
"If we miss the bus, we can't go to camp, right?"

76
00:08:28.607 --> 00:08:32.646
Iris gasped. "Mama will be so mad!"

77
00:08:32.647 --> 00:08:39.950
"I know," Javier said. "But she'll be on her way to work. She might not even know."

78
00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:48.753
"Javier!" Iris was already speeding back toward the apartment building. "We have to get our lunches—now!"

79
00:08:49.494 --> 00:08:56.989
Just as Iris got to the front stoop, though, Mama stormed out the front door, their lunches in her hands.

80
00:08:58.054 --> 00:09:01.422
"You forgot your—" She halted.

81
00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:05.203
Iris and Javier followed Mama's gaze down the block.

82
00:09:05.564 --> 00:09:20.755
The camp bus was pulling away from the curb and picking up speed, leaving them behind.
